  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening capacities of National institutions in Ecuador in identifying and managing cultural and natural heritage</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In close cooperation with the national authorities of Ecuador, in particular the Ministry of Culture and Heritage, the National Cultural Heritage Institute (INPC), and the Ministry of Environment, Water and Ecological Transition, a series of training activities will be conducted on the use of the 1972 World Heritage Convention to identify local strategies to support the protection and preservation of cultural and natural heritage:

-Training workshops with the participation of the Decentralized Autonomous Governments of Ecuador (regional, provincial, and cantonal GADs) to identify at a first level the cultural, natural, and mixed properties that have the potential to be inscribed on the World Heritage List.
-National workshop with the participation of international experts and Advisory Bodies of the Convention to examine the results of the process.
-Identification of properties that will constitute the World Heritage Tentative List of Ecuador.</narrative>
  </description>
